acceptance "Remaining tasks: lock dialect/compiler/ABI matrix; lower values/control/errors/\nresources with explicit overflow/shift/narrowing behavior; generate helpers and\nfreestanding/hosted dependency records; compile/run positive fixtures and reject\nmissing provenance, hidden libc/allocator and unsafe assumptions. Yes/no: do\nresults and diagnostics agree with Gravity, is safe code free of target UB, and\nare helper dependencies explicit? Evidence: [C manifest assembly](../../bootstrap/clojure/src/gravity/bootstrap_impl/semantic_late/140134-c-backend-manifest.clj)\nrecords source, dialect, plan, execution and provenance inputs, not full C\nconformance. Decision owner: C maintainer; recommendation: preserve the contract's\nexplicit freestanding C11 versus hosted C17 distinction. Integrates Lower,\nRuntime and Emit; C expansion does not gate the selected LLVM candidate.", :component "backends", :source-path "specs/backends-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "backend-c", :canonical-marker "backends-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/backends-workflow/tasks.md" "backends-implementation-tasks" "backend-llvm"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "62635384fb49256f61776d64827abb86b2179cf2f34b8349c4909e9338bb23a0", :state :open, :acceptance "Remaining tasks: reconcile the selected Linux candidate with the full target\ncontract without changing its selection; implement missing operation/layout/\natomic/error/FFI mappings; admit attributes only from matching proofs; run LLVM\nverification, real native execution and missing-proof/poison/target-mismatch\nrejection; attach reproducibility and debug/provenance evidence. Yes/no: are\nattributes justified, undefined/poison shortcuts absent, target facts pinned\nand emitted artifacts executable? Evidence: [Linux artifact implementation](../../bootstrap/clojure/src/gravity/bootstrap_impl/semantic_llvm/036-linux-artifact-record.clj).\nDecision owner: LLVM maintainer; recommendation: retain the adopted Linux\ncandidate and treat additional triples as explicit family extensions, not\nsilent release-target substitution. Integrates Lower/Emit/Runtime. The selected\ncandidate is a stage of this broader outcome, not evidence of all LLVM targets.", :component "backends", :source-path "specs/backends-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "backend-llvm", :canonical-marker "backends-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/backends-workflow/tasks.md" "backends-implementation-tasks" "backend-wasm"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "62635384fb49256f61776d64827abb86b2179cf2f34b8349c4909e9338bb23a0", :state :open, :acceptance "Remaining tasks: record core/component/embedder target matrix; implement memory,\nresource-handle and canonical ABI lowering; implement typed async stream/future\ncompletion/cancellation/backpressure for claimed async targets; generate/import\nbindings; validate and execute modules with bounds, missing-grant, unsupported-\nfeature, resource-lifetime and replay rejection fixtures. Yes/no: are exports\nschema-correct, imports authorized, resource lifetimes enforced and selected\nfeatures actually supported? Evidence: [feature mapping](../../bootstrap/clojure/src/gravity/bootstrap_impl/components/backends/00231-b4-document-feature-requirement.clj)\nis document coverage, not a working component runtime. Decision owner: Wasm\nmaintainer; recommendation: explicit core versus component acceptance tracks and\npinned embedder versions; do not treat synchronous core support as async-component\ncompletion. Parallel to LLVM; integrates Schema/Auth/Runtime and Emit.", :component "backends", :source-path "specs/backends-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "backend-wasm", :canonical-marker "backends-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/backends-workflow/tasks.md" "backends-implementation-tasks" "backend-jvm"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "62635384fb49256f61776d64827abb86b2179cf2f34b8349c4909e9338bb23a0", :state :open, :acceptance "Remaining tasks: fix supported JVM/classloader/package matrix; complete bytecode\nand interop lowering; enforce nullability, exception translation, deterministic\nlinear cleanup and dynamic-use grants; execute packaged programs and reject\nungranted reflection/native access, unchecked null and missing metadata. Yes/no:\ndo real class/JAR artifacts execute, do host boundaries preserve semantics, and\nare cleanup/grants enforced? Evidence: [JVM manifest assembly](../../bootstrap/clojure/src/gravity/bootstrap_impl/semantic_late/142709-jvm-backend-manifest.clj)\nconsumes class/JAR and execution fields; inspection is not execution proof.\nDecision owner: JVM maintainer; recommendation: a pinned baseline classfile/JVM\npair plus explicit compatibility matrix. Integrates managed Runtime and Build;\nthis hosted path does not replace the selected native release.", :component "backends", :source-path "specs/backends-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "backend-jvm", :canonical-marker "backends-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/backends-workflow/tasks.md" "backends-implementation-tasks" "backend-js"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "62635384fb49256f61776d64827abb86b2179cf2f34b8349c4909e9338bb23a0", :state :open, :acceptance "Remaining tasks: declare Node/browser/edge adapter matrix; lower numeric and\ncontrol/resource semantics; generate declarations and checked null/undefined/\npromise adapters; preserve source maps/package side-effect policy; execute\nprograms and reject unauthorized globals, lossy numeric conversions and unsafe\nimports. Yes/no: do exports match declarations, numeric modes survive, host\nvalues are validated and denied globals stay inaccessible? Evidence:\n[JS manifest assembly](../../bootstrap/clojure/src/gravity/bootstrap_impl/semantic_late/141626-js-ts-backend-manifest.clj)\nexplicitly records Node host globals; it does not establish every JS environment.\nDecision owner: JS maintainer; recommendation: separate runtime adapters sharing\none semantic lowering layer. Parallel to JVM/LLVM; integrates Schema/Runtime/UI.", :component "backends", :source-path "specs/backends-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "backend-js", :canonical-marker "backends-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/backends-workflow/tasks.md" "backends-implementation-tasks" "backend-mlir"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "62635384fb49256f61776d64827abb86b2179cf2f34b8349c4909e9338bb23a0", :state :open, :acceptance "Remaining tasks: pin MLIR version/dialects and operation coverage; implement\ntypes/effects/ownership/proof attributes and verifiers; implement conversions and\nmetadata-preservation checks; run actual verification/conversion and reject\nillegal targets or fact loss. Yes/no: do modules verify, conversions preserve\nfacts and downstream consumers accept the result? Evidence:\n[MLIR manifest](../../bootstrap/clojure/src/gravity/bootstrap_impl/components/backends/00244-b7-document-mlir-manifest.clj)\nuses `stage0-recorded` version and a narrow operation map; nested complete flags\nare not tool execution. Decision owner: MLIR maintainer; recommendation: explicit\nversioned dialect registry and legal conversion pipeline. Optional MLIR use\nmust not become a prerequisite for backends that do not require it.", :component "backends", :source-path "specs/backends-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "backend-mlir", :canonical-marker "backends-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/backends-workflow/tasks.md" "backends-implementation-tasks" "backend-gpu"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "62635384fb49256f61776d64827abb86b2179cf2f34b8349c4909e9338bb23a0", :state :open, :acceptance "Remaining tasks: adopt API/device/toolchain matrix; implement kernel emission\nand argument ABI; generate explicit transfer/launch/cleanup stubs; execute real\nor declared simulator kernels and reject host-only effects, invalid barriers,\nimplicit transfers and uncertified relaxed math. Yes/no: do kernels run, buffer\nlifetimes hold, synchronization matches IR and numeric results meet mode?\nEvidence: [GPU manifest](../../bootstrap/clojure/src/gravity/bootstrap_impl/components/backends/00248-b8-document-gpu-manifest.clj)\nrecords a SPIR-V-shaped fixture, not device execution. Decision owner: GPU\nmaintainer; recommendation: one explicit reference API/device pair first with\nnamed additional target obligations. Integrates GPU domain/Runtime/Emit;\naccelerator availability does not gate the ordinary compiler release.", :component "backends", :source-path "specs/backends-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "backend-gpu", :canonical-marker "backends-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/backends-workflow/tasks.md" "backends-implementation-tasks" "backend-hdl"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "62635384fb49256f61776d64827abb86b2179cf2f34b8349c4909e9338bb23a0", :state :open, :acceptance "Remaining tasks: adopt HDL/toolchain and synthesis target record; implement\nstate/port/memory lowering and explicit width behavior; preserve clock/reset\ncrossing proofs; generate testbenches and simulate/synthesize; reject hidden\nruntime, illegal crossings and unrepresentable hardware behavior. Yes/no: does\nHDL synthesize, do cycle traces match source, and are width/reset/crossing rules\nenforced? Evidence: [HDL module fixture](../../bootstrap/clojure/src/gravity/bootstrap_impl/components/backends/00251-b9-document-hdl-module.clj)\nis a fixed string, not general lowering. Decision owner: hardware emitter\nmaintainer; recommendation: explicit SystemVerilog reference flow, subject to\narchitecture adoption and tool availability. Hardware IR is prerequisite for\nintegration; neither fabrication nor a completed OS is required for emitter work.", :component "backends", :source-path "specs/backends-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "backend-hdl", :canonical-marker "backends-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/backends-workflow/tasks.md" "backends-implementation-tasks" "backend-workflow"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "62635384fb49256f61776d64827abb86b2179cf2f34b8349c4909e9338bb23a0", :state :open, :acceptance "Remaining tasks: implement graph/provider lowering; emit schemas and replay/\nidempotency policy; encode retry/compensation/review transitions; run emitted\ngraphs through a declared runtime including restart/replay; reject unrecorded\nnondeterminism, missing review and repeated external effects. Yes/no: can the\ngraph resume/replay correctly, are external effects guarded and origins retained?\nEvidence: [workflow graph fixture](../../bootstrap/clojure/src/gravity/bootstrap_impl/components/backends/00255-b10-document-workflow-graph.clj)\nis fixed graph/event text, not general executable lowering. Decision owner:\ngraph maintainer; recommendation: provider-neutral graph plus a versioned runtime\nadapter. Parallel to native backends; depends on Workflow/Schema/Auth interfaces.", :component "backends", :source-path "specs/backends-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "backend-workflow", :canonical-marker "backends-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/backends-workflow/tasks.md" "backends-implementation-tasks" "backend-ai"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "62635384fb49256f61776d64827abb86b2179cf2f34b8349c4909e9338bb23a0", :state :open, :acceptance "Remaining tasks: implement AI artifact/provider binding; emit structured-output,\ntaint and human-review boundary records; connect workflow/runtime adapters;\nexecute accepted model/tool fixtures and reject injection, wrong provider,\nmissing review and unvalidated output; bind evaluations to emitted identities.\nYes/no: do artifacts execute only permitted actions, preserve schema/taint and\nreview, and retain exact model/prompt/tool provenance? Baseline evidence:\n[workflow graph fixture](../../bootstrap/clojure/src/gravity/bootstrap_impl/components/backends/00255-b10-document-workflow-graph.clj)\ncontains model/tool/review nodes but proves no live provider completion.\nDecision owner: AI adapter maintainer; recommendation: provider-neutral artifacts\nwith explicit adapters, not a vendor SDK as semantics. Integrates AI domain,\nWorkflow/Schema/Auth/Runtime; no live model call is required for unrelated builds.", :component "backends", :source-path "specs/backends-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "backend-ai", :canonical-marker "backends-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/backends-workflow/tasks.md" "backends-implementation-tasks" "backend-query"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "62635384fb49256f61776d64827abb86b2179cf2f34b8349c4909e9338bb23a0", :state :open, :acceptance "Remaining tasks: adopt dialect/provider matrix; implement parameterized lowering\nand null/collation/numeric mappings; generate row/transaction/migration adapters;\nexecute queries and reject tainted SQL, unauthorized writes, schema drift and\nunapproved data loss. Yes/no: do rows match types, parameterization survive and\ntransactions/migrations respect policy? Evidence:\n[query fixtures](../../bootstrap/clojure/src/gravity/bootstrap_impl/components/backends/00259-b11-document-validate-source-overrides.clj)\ncontain one parameterized select and no-op migration, not general query support.\nDecision owner: relational maintainer; recommendation: one explicit dialect\nadapter with provider/version records, then separate conformance per extension.\nIntegrates Query domain/Schema/Runtime; no database service gates compiler bootstrap.", :component "backends", :source-path "specs/backends-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "backend-query", :canonical-marker "backends-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/backends-workflow/tasks.md" "backends-implementation-tasks" "backend-mobile"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "62635384fb49256f61776d64827abb86b2179cf2f34b8349c4909e9338bb23a0", :state :open, :acceptance "Remaining tasks: adopt platform/version/package matrix; implement typed platform\nbindings and UI/lifecycle/threading adapters; emit resources/permissions and\npackage metadata; run simulator/device apps and reject absent permissions,\nwrong-thread UI, invalid lifecycle use and hidden background work; attach source\nmaps/store-audit records. Yes/no: does the bundle launch, do lifecycle and denial\npaths execute correctly, and are host values/errors normalized? Evidence:\n[mobile fixture](../../bootstrap/clojure/src/gravity/bootstrap_impl/components/backends/00263-b12-document-app-bundle.clj)\nis an iOS-shaped string validated by substring checks, not an actual app bundle.\nDecision owner: mobile maintainer; recommendation: independent iOS and Android\nadapters and explicit simulator/device evidence, not one generic mobile claim.\nIntegrates UI/Runtime/Emit/Build; external signing/store publication remains a\nseparate authorized action and does not gate unrelated compiler components.", :component "backends", :source-path "specs/backends-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "backend-mobile", :canonical-marker "backends-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/backends-workflow/tasks.md" "backends-implementation-tasks" "backend-emission"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "62635384fb49256f61776d64827abb86b2179cf2f34b8349c4909e9338bb23a0", :state :open, :acceptance "Remaining tasks: implement common record/schema checks across all artifact\nkinds; bind hashes and provenance to actual bytes and dependencies; enforce\nmissing/stale/contradictory evidence rejection; attach per-family conformance\npacks before package/release consumers. Yes/no: do records identify real bytes,\nall required edges exist and tampering/staleness reject? Evidence:\n[emission contract implementation](../../bootstrap/clojure/src/gravity/bootstrap_impl/semantic_early/26010-artifact-emission-contract-and-backend-inputs.clj)\nassembles required records; existence is not family execution evidence. Decision\nowner: artifact maintainer; recommendation: one versioned envelope with\nkind-specific validation. Independent family fixtures may develop in parallel;\nBuild/Release consume accepted records later.", :component "backends", :source-path "specs/backends-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "backend-emission", :canonical-marker "backends-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/backends-workflow/tasks.md" "backends-implementation-tasks" "backend-conformance"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "62635384fb49256f61776d64827abb86b2179cf2f34b8349c4909e9338bb23a0", :state :open, :acceptance "Remaining tasks: reconcile canonical operation/domain fixture matrix; implement\nfamily adapters and exact rejection assertions; execute or semantically compare\nreal outputs; check evidence/provenance preservation and nondeterminism replay;\nrecord unavailable targets explicitly without converting skips to passes;\npublish exact-source family coverage. Yes/no: does each claim have positive and\nnegative execution evidence, are metadata checks independent of result equality,\nand are unavailable targets honestly open? Evidence:\n[existing test-matrix artifact](../../bootstrap/clojure/src/gravity/bootstrap_impl/components/backends/00224-backend-test-matrix-file-artifact.clj)\nis a starting integration surface, not acceptance. Decision owner: conformance\nmaintainer; recommendation: shared fixture semantics plus target-specific runners,\nwith explicit availability records. Conformance interface work is parallel;\nfamily acceptance awaits its actual backend. No automatic release closure follows.", :component "backends", :source-path "specs/backends-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "backend-conformance", :canonical-marker "backends-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/build-workflow/tasks.md" "build-implementation-tasks" "build/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-projectlock-normalization-and-constraint-resolution"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "675a71a78bb4628fc680987cf7074047370f0bbec3e61d82e46e300cd79cb39e", :state :open, :acceptance "Real dependency resolution with conflict, profile and capability rejection", :component "build", :source-path "specs/build-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "build/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-projectlock-normalization-and-constraint-resolution", :canonical-marker "build-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/build-workflow/tasks.md" "build-implementation-tasks" "build/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/execute-typed-graph-under-declared-build-effects"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "675a71a78bb4628fc680987cf7074047370f0bbec3e61d82e46e300cd79cb39e", :state :open, :acceptance "Clean build node receipts and undeclared environment/network/shell rejection", :component "build", :source-path "specs/build-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "build/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/execute-typed-graph-under-declared-build-effects", :canonical-marker "build-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/build-workflow/tasks.md" "build-implementation-tasks" "build/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-dependency-aware-caching-and-invalidation"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "675a71a78bb4628fc680987cf7074047370f0bbec3e61d82e46e300cd79cb39e", :state :open, :acceptance "Reuse on equal inputs; rebuild on source, compiler, grant, policy or target changes", :component "build", :source-path "specs/build-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "build/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-dependency-aware-caching-and-invalidation", :canonical-marker "build-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/build-workflow/tasks.md" "build-implementation-tasks" "build/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/produce-and-verify-packageprovenancesigning-records"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "675a71a78bb4628fc680987cf7074047370f0bbec3e61d82e46e300cd79cb39e", :state :open, :acceptance "Actual published package retrieval/verification fixtures; tamper and missing-record rejection", :component "build", :source-path "specs/build-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "build/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/produce-and-verify-packageprovenancesigning-records", :canonical-marker "build-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/build-workflow/tasks.md" "build-implementation-tasks" "build/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/close-reproducibility-and-target-matrix"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "675a71a78bb4628fc680987cf7074047370f0bbec3e61d82e46e300cd79cb39e", :state :open, :acceptance "Repeated locked builds with matching identities and explicit failing-target diagnostics", :component "build", :source-path "specs/build-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "build/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/close-reproducibility-and-target-matrix", :canonical-marker "build-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/cli-workflow/tasks.md" "cli-implementation-tasks" "cli/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/reconcile-supported-commandoptions-with-normative-families"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "75300e2d2d3c9a44e0799ee203d3126eeba690adbbd89f0dcc8b4bbf4c7a88c7", :state :open, :acceptance "Command matrix that distinguishes implemented, rejected and unavailable operations", :component "cli", :source-path "specs/cli-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "cli/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/reconcile-supported-commandoptions-with-normative-families", :canonical-marker "cli-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/cli-workflow/tasks.md" "cli-implementation-tasks" "cli/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/connect-checkruncompilebuildtestpackageverify-to-real-services"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "75300e2d2d3c9a44e0799ee203d3126eeba690adbbd89f0dcc8b4bbf4c7a88c7", :state :open, :acceptance "Executed success/failure fixtures and artifact paths at public command boundary", :component "cli", :source-path "specs/cli-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "cli/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/connect-checkruncompilebuildtestpackageverify-to-real-services", :canonical-marker "cli-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/cli-workflow/tasks.md" "cli-implementation-tasks" "cli/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/connect-replformatlintdocinspectprofileauditairegistryexplain-services"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "75300e2d2d3c9a44e0799ee203d3126eeba690adbbd89f0dcc8b4bbf4c7a88c7", :state :open, :acceptance "Each declared command has a genuine service result and negative fixture; no metadata-only success", :component "cli", :source-path "specs/cli-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "cli/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/connect-replformatlintdocinspectprofileauditairegistryexplain-services", :canonical-marker "cli-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/cli-workflow/tasks.md" "cli-implementation-tasks" "cli/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/normalize-json-text-exit-codes-and-redaction"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "75300e2d2d3c9a44e0799ee203d3126eeba690adbbd89f0dcc8b4bbf4c7a88c7", :state :open, :acceptance "Golden success/error outputs including source, target, grants and redacted secrets", :component "cli", :source-path "specs/cli-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "cli/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/normalize-json-text-exit-codes-and-redaction", :canonical-marker "cli-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/cli-workflow/tasks.md" "cli-implementation-tasks" "cli/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/package-and-verify-user-entrypoints"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "75300e2d2d3c9a44e0799ee203d3126eeba690adbbd89f0dcc8b4bbf4c7a88c7", :state :open, :acceptance "Installed invocation, source-extension provenance and unsupported-option rejection", :component "cli", :source-path "specs/cli-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "cli/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/package-and-verify-user-entrypoints", :canonical-marker "cli-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/compiler-api-workflow/tasks.md" "compiler-api-implementation-tasks" "pipeline"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "e051d2c8f5bc21b03600db509f6fb570840a4359bfa4e4cc7d5d247bc5231da0", :state :open, :acceptance "Owner role: compiler API/pipeline maintainer. All tasks open; source evidence\nabove is partial implementation evidence, not closure.\n\n| Task | Concrete closing evidence |\n| --- | --- |\n| Stabilize public request/context/result API | Versioned schema and compatibility fixtures for source and stage-artifact calls; missing versions, incompatible schemas and hidden mutable-context access reject. A direct caller and CLI adapter receive the same semantic results. |\n| Register and schedule actual passes | Built-in registration binds implementation/version to complete requires/preserves/invalidates/regenerates/effects/profile contracts; execute declared order and reject missing facts, duplicate/conflicting registration and illegal ordering before consumption. |\n| Execute and retain stage products | Actual selected compiler invocation records input/output identities, diagnostics, source origins and provenance for every required stage, including fused-pass observable boundaries; verifier failure stops downstream execution. |\n| Derive cache keys and invalidate facts | Use actual source/compiler/pass/plugin/grant/replay/policy/target inputs; unchanged-input reuse agrees with a clean run, and every contract invalidation class triggers revalidation or recomputation. Stale proofs, diagnostics and speculative release reuse reject. |\n| Integrate compiler consumers | Build, CLI and inspection callers consume the same API artifacts; positive and negative selected-target programs demonstrate no raw/unchecked backend input and no runnable output from diagnostic-only mode. |\n\nYes/no acceptance: are passes actually invoked? Are all required stage facts\nverified and retained? Are clean and reused results semantically equivalent?\nAre stale inputs and invalid stage orders rejected? Does public API behavior\nremain independent of ambient mutable compiler state? All must be yes.", :component "compiler-api", :source-path "specs/compiler-api-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "pipeline", :canonical-marker "compiler-api-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/compiler-api-workflow/tasks.md" "compiler-api-implementation-tasks" "plugins"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "e051d2c8f5bc21b03600db509f6fb570840a4359bfa4e4cc7d5d247bc5231da0", :state :open, :acceptance "Owner role: compiler extension-host maintainer. All tasks open.\n\n| Task | Concrete closing evidence |\n| --- | --- |\n| Check manifest compatibility before code loading | Actual loader validates package identity, API/compiler version, declared passes/artifacts, trust and grants; incompatible/malformed/rejected packages produce diagnostics without executing initialization code. |\n| Execute scoped plugin context | Run a deterministic read-only analysis and authorized transformation through actual scoped IR APIs; read-only writes, unauthorized namespaces/phases and hidden compiler mutation reject at the operation boundary. |\n| Enforce real sandbox/build-effect boundaries | Exercise sandboxed and policy-trusted plugin execution; filesystem/network/process/environment/model/tool/artifact operations without grants are denied before effects, including host escape paths. Trust labels alone do not disable scoped checks. |\n| Register passes, facets and domain interfaces | Require declared schema, verifier, profile support, effects, lowering path and conformance records as applicable; execute registered schema/verifier callbacks and reject opaque, conflicting or unauthorized registration. Component owners retain domain semantics. |\n| Verify output, trace execution and revalidate reuse | Run the declared output verifier, reject invalid transformed artifacts, record actual plugin/package/grant/input/output/replay identities, and invalidate cache entries on changed versions, policy or dependencies. |\n\nYes/no acceptance: can incompatible plugin initialization run? Can a plugin\nperform ungranted effects or mutate hidden state? Can an invalid output enter\nthe pipeline? All must be no. Are allowed sandboxed/trusted invocations real,\ntraceable and reproducible under their declared replay policy? Must be yes.", :component "compiler-api", :source-path "specs/compiler-api-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "plugins", :canonical-marker "compiler-api-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/compiler-api-workflow/tasks.md" "compiler-api-implementation-tasks" "pass-evidence"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "e051d2c8f5bc21b03600db509f6fb570840a4359bfa4e4cc7d5d247bc5231da0", :state :open, :acceptance "Owner role: compiler verification maintainer. All tasks open.\n\n| Task | Concrete closing evidence |\n| --- | --- |\n| Classify real pass population | Enumerate every pass in the declared compiler closure with version, risk, affected profiles/targets and governing minimum evidence; reject omitted passes or incompatible evidence classes. |\n| Execute required verification gates | Invoke actual schema/semantic verifiers at required compiler boundaries; bind reports to input/output identity and stop affected artifact production on failure rather than accepting supplied success flags. |\n| Bind transformation evidence | Changed MIR functions receive the governing translation validation or checked proof evidence; check-elision proofs/certificates are checked, and target lowering has actual differential/backend conformance receipts for claimed targets. |\n| Capture failures and preserve trust boundaries | Record counterexample input/output/property/diagnostic and source identities, retain the prior valid artifact after rejected transformation, and turn reproducible failures into regression fixtures. |\n| Emit truthful trust and release-gate records | Reports enumerate supported profiles/targets, residual evidence gaps and experimental gates; missing/high-risk/stale evidence blocks affected release artifacts. Release consumes this decision but independently owns final acceptance. |\n\nYes/no acceptance: do reports derive from actual checks on exact artifacts?\nAre plugin and backend passes included when used? Are absent evidence and\ncounterexamples visible? Do failures block the affected claimed release path?\nAll must be yes. No claim of a fully mechanized compiler is implied.", :component "compiler-api", :source-path "specs/compiler-api-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "pass-evidence", :canonical-marker "compiler-api-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/compiler-api-workflow/tasks.md" "compiler-api-implementation-tasks" "development-boundaries"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "e051d2c8f5bc21b03600db509f6fb570840a4359bfa4e4cc7d5d247bc5231da0", :state :open, :acceptance "Owner role: compiler development infrastructure maintainer. Current acceptance unassessed.\nThis is the new task-authority record for the existing SH-01 delivery, not a\nclaim of missing implementation or another pipeline/pass-evidence task. The\noriginal accepted E01 scope and four-test/57-assertion report remain historical\ncompletion at `cbc55cd1477deca08a9c042c91db98005833021a`; the\n[source-pinned audit](https://github.com/burn2delete/uniform/blob/15a5499e97798621d270c36dd2546ce98ddd62a9/docs/self-hosting-sh00-sh06-evidence-audit.md)\nretains the later S-after-repair qualifications. Open tracks unassessed current\nacceptance, and does not reopen the historically completed implementation.\n\n| Task | Concrete closing evidence |\n| --- | --- |\n| Publish semantic module and API ownership | One actual semantic owner for each compiler stage and public API; total source-pinned ownership projection with duplicate and missing-owner rejection. |\n| Preserve fixture and shared-routing ownership | Fixture, test, artifact-generation, coverage and shared dispatch paths have explicit owners; executable shared files have no competing semantic writers. |\n| Permit dedicated focused tests | Add and select a focused owning test without unrelated changes to the monolithic bootstrap namespace; retain the actual dedicated discovery result. |\n| Delegate compatibility entrypoints | Compatibility wrappers call the owning implementation; representative checks reject a second semantic implementation hidden behind an adapter. |\n| Select affected verification truthfully | Exact namespace/selector selection covers affected callers and rejects unknown selectors; failed, interrupted and skipped results retain their actual disposition. |\n| Verify representative ownership boundaries | Source-pinned leaf and shared changes exercise routing and ownership with affected checks, without unrelated compiler modifications. |\n\nYes/no acceptance: are semantic and fixture/shared-path owners total and unique,\ndedicated test changes possible, compatibility entrypoints delegated, affected\nselectors strict, and representative leaf/shared changes verified? All must be\nyes for current acceptance. Preserve historical completion at its original scope.\nStop at this existing boundary; no new coordination framework, compiler feature,\nmass refactor, per-change admission wrapper or task-count gate is required.", :component "compiler-api", :source-path "specs/compiler-api-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "development-boundaries", :canonical-marker "compiler-api-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/core-workflow/tasks.md" "core-implementation-tasks" "core/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/core1-lower-core-forms"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "e719f4d797af9e25867f5248a148f7698068e9ef7e50dcc7f1e3c25622dc1e97", :state :open, :acceptance "Implement quote, if, do, let, fn, loop/recur, def, var, set!, try/throw and match with specified evaluation order and shape validation.", :component "core", :source-path "specs/core-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open; partial source evidence above is not closure", :id "core/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/core1-lower-core-forms", :canonical-marker "core-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/core-workflow/tasks.md" "core-implementation-tasks" "core/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/core2-preserve-binding-structure"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "e719f4d797af9e25867f5248a148f7698068e9ef7e50dcc7f1e3c25622dc1e97", :state :open, :acceptance "Represent lexical identity, closure captures, recursion and mutation explicitly; attach resolved references before downstream typed-core acceptance.", :component "core", :source-path "specs/core-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open; partial source evidence above is not closure", :id "core/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/core2-preserve-binding-structure", :canonical-marker "core-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/core-workflow/tasks.md" "core-implementation-tasks" "core/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/core3-desugar-without-semantic-loss"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "e719f4d797af9e25867f5248a148f7698068e9ef7e50dcc7f1e3c25622dc1e97", :state :open, :acceptance "Lower surface conveniences while recording source/generated origins, effects, capabilities, metadata and unsafe declarations.", :component "core", :source-path "specs/core-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open; partial source evidence above is not closure", :id "core/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/core3-desugar-without-semantic-loss", :canonical-marker "core-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/core-workflow/tasks.md" "core-implementation-tasks" "core/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/core4-verify-and-serialize"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "e719f4d797af9e25867f5248a148f7698068e9ef7e50dcc7f1e3c25622dc1e97", :state :open, :acceptance "Reject malformed node graphs, illegal control positions, unresolved required bindings and lost origins; round-trip valid modules.", :component "core", :source-path "specs/core-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open; partial source evidence above is not closure", :id "core/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/core4-verify-and-serialize", :canonical-marker "core-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/core-workflow/tasks.md" "core-implementation-tasks" "core/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/core5-integrate-semantic-analyses"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "e719f4d797af9e25867f5248a148f7698068e9ef7e50dcc7f1e3c25622dc1e97", :state :open, :acceptance "Use the same core interface for handwritten/generated input and feed Types/Effects with accepted control-flow programs and rejected malformed/illegal core fixtures.", :component "core", :source-path "specs/core-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open; partial source evidence above is not closure", :id "core/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/core5-integrate-semantic-analyses", :canonical-marker "core-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/diag-workflow/tasks.md" "diag-implementation-tasks" "diag/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/reconcile-stage-carriers-with-canonical-record-schema"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "a4b029e285344368079a3120f387217c01468fbc11f24aff8cf219c9284128b4", :state :open, :acceptance "Record/schema parity fixtures from each producer, including malformed-record rejection", :component "diag", :source-path "specs/diag-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "diag/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/reconcile-stage-carriers-with-canonical-record-schema", :canonical-marker "diag-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/diag-workflow/tasks.md" "diag-implementation-tasks" "diag/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/preserve-primaryrelatedgenerated-origins-and-stable-order"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "a4b029e285344368079a3120f387217c01468fbc11f24aff8cf219c9284128b4", :state :open, :acceptance "Macro and optimized-source diagnostics with original and generated locations", :component "diag", :source-path "specs/diag-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "diag/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/preserve-primaryrelatedgenerated-origins-and-stable-order", :canonical-marker "diag-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/diag-workflow/tasks.md" "diag-implementation-tasks" "diag/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/close-textjsonredaction-and-explain-contracts"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "a4b029e285344368079a3120f387217c01468fbc11f24aff8cf219c9284128b4", :state :open, :acceptance "Golden text/JSON equivalence, secret redaction and known-ID explanation", :component "diag", :source-path "specs/diag-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "diag/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/close-textjsonredaction-and-explain-contracts", :canonical-marker "diag-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/diag-workflow/tasks.md" "diag-implementation-tasks" "diag/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/integrate-runtimebuildeditor-consumers-without-rule-drift"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "a4b029e285344368079a3120f387217c01468fbc11f24aff8cf219c9284128b4", :state :open, :acceptance "Same underlying diagnostic identity across public consumers and failure paths", :component "diag", :source-path "specs/diag-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "diag/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/integrate-runtimebuildeditor-consumers-without-rule-drift", :canonical-marker "diag-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/domains-workflow/tasks.md" "domains-implementation-tasks" "math"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "ac5436b11b3d5a9918c4471a9237fd9f8358eadd3f242abed78c7a7fe92d7cd4", :state :open, :acceptance "Outcome: [math contracts](../../docs/phase-05-mathematical-and-elementary-function-system/README.md) execute with the declared\nnumeric semantics and checked justification for transformations. Remaining\nfinite tasks, all open: implement numeric-mode/domain checking; implement EFIR\nlowering and evaluation; connect EML/certificate checking to justified rewrites;\nimplement certified approximation/interval and symbolic operations; run the\ncontract conformance matrix with rejected unproved transformations.\n\nYes/no acceptance: do domain and branch errors reject? Do proof-dependent\nrewrites require checked evidence? Do strict-mode results match the selected\nsemantics? Integration: Types/MIR to EFIR, Opt proof preservation, Lower/Stdlib\nnumeric APIs. Decision owner: numeric maintainer; recommendation: keep EML as\nadjacent proof/search representation, never ordinary runtime equality authority.", :component "domains", :source-path "specs/domains-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "math", :canonical-marker "domains-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/domains-workflow/tasks.md" "domains-implementation-tasks" "schema"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "ac5436b11b3d5a9918c4471a9237fd9f8358eadd3f242abed78c7a7fe92d7cd4", :state :open, :acceptance "Outcome: generated consumers enforce the same source schema. Remaining tasks,\nall open: implement schema normalization and validators; implement canonical\nserialization and version identities; generate GraphQL/OpenAPI and ABI/config\nartifacts; implement checked migration mapping; execute source/generated parity\nand weakening/taint/invalid-data rejection fixtures.\n\nYes/no acceptance: is schema identity stable? Do generated consumers reject\ninvalid values? Are migration loss and secret exposure prevented or explicitly\nrejected? Integration: Types to schema, Emit generated artifacts, Build schema\nidentity, Query/AI/Stdlib consumers. Decision owner: schema maintainer;\nrecommendation: shared canonical schema IR with explicit target adapters.", :component "domains", :source-path "specs/domains-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "schema", :canonical-marker "domains-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/domains-workflow/tasks.md" "domains-implementation-tasks" "query"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "ac5436b11b3d5a9918c4471a9237fd9f8358eadd3f242abed78c7a7fe92d7cd4", :state :open, :acceptance "Outcome: real parameterized queries return validated rows and respect declared\ntransaction/provider semantics. Remaining tasks, all open: implement relational\nIR and typed parameters; lower to a declared provider; connect row/schema and\ntransaction checks; execute result-equivalence, injection, missing-grant and\ninvalid-row fixtures. Yes/no acceptance: are parameters separated from query\nsyntax? Are results typed and grants enforced? Do transaction failures preserve\nsemantics? Integration: Schema/MIR to Query, Runtime provider, Stdlib database\nAPI. Decision owner: query maintainer; recommendation: explicit provider dialect\ncontract, not host SQL strings as semantic authority.", :component "domains", :source-path "specs/domains-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "query", :canonical-marker "domains-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/domains-workflow/tasks.md" "domains-implementation-tasks" "workflow"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "ac5436b11b3d5a9918c4471a9237fd9f8358eadd3f242abed78c7a7fe92d7cd4", :state :open, :acceptance "Outcome: a workflow executes and replays without repeating recorded external\neffects. Remaining tasks, all open: implement graph validation/lowering;\nimplement event-log schema and durable transitions; connect retry/compensation/\ntimer providers; execute crash/restart/replay and unrecorded-nondeterminism\nrejection fixtures. Yes/no acceptance: is replay deterministic? Are external\ncalls deduplicated? Are invalid transitions rejected? Integration: MIR/Schema,\nRuntime durability, AI review steps, Stdlib workflows. Decision owner: workflow\nmaintainer; recommendation: versioned event log as replay input, explicit\nprovider boundary for storage rather than a hidden database choice.", :component "domains", :source-path "specs/domains-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "workflow", :canonical-marker "domains-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/domains-workflow/tasks.md" "domains-implementation-tasks" "ai"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "ac5436b11b3d5a9918c4471a9237fd9f8358eadd3f242abed78c7a7fe92d7cd4", :state :open, :acceptance "Outcome: the declared AI workflow executes through schema, capability, taint\nand human-review boundaries. Remaining tasks, all open: implement declaration\nlowering; connect model/tool/memory providers with explicit policies; implement\nstructured-output and taint validation; connect human review and replay;\nexecute evaluations plus prompt-injection, missing-review, cross-tenant and\nunvalidated-output rejection fixtures. Yes/no acceptance: does untrusted output\nremain data? Are actions denied without grants/review? Are evaluations bound to\nexact prompt/model/tool identities? Integration: Schema/Auth, Workflow/Runtime,\nStdlib AI. Decision owner: AI maintainer; recommendation: provider-independent\nartifacts and explicit model identity, never a vendor SDK side path.", :component "domains", :source-path "specs/domains-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "ai", :canonical-marker "domains-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/domains-workflow/tasks.md" "domains-implementation-tasks" "gpu"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "ac5436b11b3d5a9918c4471a9237fd9f8358eadd3f242abed78c7a7fe92d7cd4", :state :open, :acceptance "Outcome: kernels execute on the adopted target with validated memory/barrier\nbehavior. Remaining tasks, all open: adopt target and kernel ABI; implement GPU\nIR/checking; lower kernel and host dispatch; execute numeric/result and illegal\nmemory-space/barrier fixtures. Yes/no acceptance: do kernels produce the\nspecified results? Are invalid synchronization and target features rejected?\nIntegration: MIR/Legality, Lower/Emit, explicit Runtime dispatch. Decision owner:\naccelerator maintainer; recommendation: one named reference target first,\nadditional targets only by their own conformance evidence. Target choice is\nnot silently adopted by this roadmap.", :component "domains", :source-path "specs/domains-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "gpu", :canonical-marker "domains-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/domains-workflow/tasks.md" "domains-implementation-tasks" "ui"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "ac5436b11b3d5a9918c4471a9237fd9f8358eadd3f242abed78c7a7fe92d7cd4", :state :open, :acceptance "Outcome: an actual UI artifact renders, handles typed events and enforces\ncapabilities through the adopted adapter. Remaining tasks, all open: lock UI\nIR/state/event contract; implement lowering and rendering adapter; connect\nruntime events and source maps; execute render/update and invalid-event/unsafe\nDOM/authority rejection fixtures. Yes/no acceptance: do state transitions and\nrendering follow typed semantics? Are unsafe or unauthorized actions rejected?\nIntegration: Types/MIR, Lower/Emit, Runtime and Stdlib UI. Decision owner: UI\nmaintainer; recommendation: explicit adapter contract rather than browser host\nsemantics defining the language. Backend choice remains an explicit decision.", :component "domains", :source-path "specs/domains-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open", :id "ui", :canonical-marker "domains-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/effects-workflow/tasks.md" "effects-implementation-tasks" "effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects1-infer-direct-effects"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "af28151cd4bd37b7be8293e1a5d5385fc94e7d743a60cd45275bc0687528a3a0", :state :open, :acceptance "Classify actual core operations including allocation, IO, FFI, errors, concurrency, model/tool/memory and compile-time behavior with source references.", :component "effects", :source-path "specs/effects-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open; partial source evidence above is not closure", :id "effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects1-infer-direct-effects", :canonical-marker "effects-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/effects-workflow/tasks.md" "effects-implementation-tasks" "effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects2-propagate-latent-effects"], :checked? false, :source-sha256 "af28151cd4bd37b7be8293e1a5d5385fc94e7d743a60cd45275bc0687528a3a0", :state :open, :acceptance "Compute closure, call, dispatch and recursive-function effect summaries to a valid fixed point; distinguish declared from inferred effects.", :component "effects", :source-path "specs/effects-workflow/tasks.md", :status "Open; partial source evidence above is not closure", :id "effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects2-propagate-latent-effects", :canonical-marker "effects-implementation-tasks"} {:identity ["specs/effects-workflow/tasks.md" "effects-implementation-tasks" "effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects3-check-legality-and-ordering"], :check